# L §5.16 Closed forms: mean(e), e a sum of known multiples of random facts plus a known constant, is "the same sum of
# their means (the table below), exact or correctly rounded"; lognormal(m, s) has mean exp(m + s²/2), here exp(0.5) =
# 1.648721...: with the line's to u, 2 · 1.648721... + 1 = 4.297442... -> 4.30 (refcore prints 4.3) and the mean
# itself -> 1.6487, each correctly rounded once from the real (≈, L §7.3). (Writer 8: was REFCORE-NOT-YET, to u on a
# closed-form mean that rests on rounded values.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input ln: dist
input two: num

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  ln = lognormal(0, 1) to 1e-9
  two = 2

ask a: mean(two * ln + 1) to 0.01, mean(ln) to 0.0001
=== expect
a: (≈ 4.3 ± 0.005 (horizon none), ≈ 1.6487 ± 0.00005 (horizon none))
  cut 2026-12-31
